{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless","id":1051621,"title":"Paradox...Toothless?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-19T12:57:24-08:00","id":1051621,"title":"Paradox...Toothless?","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> We've been playing for about 16 sessions (reaching Gnosis 3 more or less across the party so 1 Arcana 4 each) so far and the few times we've had Paradox it's been contained through Wisdom for a handful of bashing bashing damage. Unleashed once as the spell was cast through an Artifact (which can't be contained) and it did some minor tweaks with only 1 success. Just now we had an attempt to Contain that failed leaving 1 Paradox success.<br /> <br /> First: the section says the number of successes increases the severity of a contained paradox failure but we don't really see anything that indicates what severities there are.<br /> <br /> Second: the player gained a paradox condition so they scoured their pattern for 1 (resistant) lethal pretty much immediately, basically bypassing the conditions effects.<br /> <br /> Outside of combat (which we're not really engaging in because Fate, Time and Space make it very much a last resort that only occurs when all other contingencies have been overcome) these bits of damage really aren't <i>that</i> much of a concern in the more narrative time of investigations, politicking and gathering resources, to the point where we players are getting pretty comfortable with reaching beyond to rolling a few paradox dice because a handful of bashing or a lethal damage isn't feeling like much of a disincentive to get silly.<br /> <br /> What are we doing wrong?<br /> <br /> I know Paradox isn't meant to be a stick to beat players over the head to stop them casting spells but it doesn't do that anyway as you can choose to cast safely by carefully controlling your Reach. I\\'m not really sure what it's <i>meant</i> to be doing now now how the rules are encouraging that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T14:01:34-08:00","id":1051657,"title":"","content":"In my experience, Paradox only really became a severe problem when I forced my players into tight spaces. Combat, subterranean labyrinths, Space-warded extradimensional temples, places like that where you're counting every turn and damage is adding up. Fate/Time/Space are tools that can be countered and tricked if your PCs have enemies that can lead them into an ambush. If you're mostly operating in narrative time, consider removing the ability to scour Paradox conditions before they lapse and just treat them as things that last for &quot;a chapter&quot; rather than in-character units of time.<br /> <br /> As for what Paradox is meant to be, I would say:<ul><li>make the session more interesting by shaking things up and complicating situations</li> <li>provide more challenges for the PCs to manage with their limited resources</li> <li>potentially keep the PCs from casting a useful spell because it's too dangerous, forcing them to use other methods</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:22:19-08:00","id":1051711,"title":"","content":"Pretty much working as intended. Ability to reliably contain Paradox is a benefit of investing into your Wisdom and keeping it healthy, which costs XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T16:15:31-08:00","id":1051731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless#post1051621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second: the player gained a paradox condition so they scoured their pattern for 1 (resistant) lethal pretty much immediately, basically bypassing the conditions effects.<br /> <br /> What are we doing wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029550-what-happens-when-a-paradox-condition-lapses?p=1029936#post1029936\">Allowing Paradox Conditions to be scoured out prematurely</a> is the big one. Regardless of the technical reading of the section, it's pretty clear the intent is that the chart for Paradox Condition Duration is supposed to actually matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T09:17:32-08:00","id":1052029,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, that's a good one, we'll be doing that, removing the Scouring option for the condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T10:40:35-08:00","id":1052050,"title":"","content":"Reading page 116(I got my hardcover only right now, so no direct quote <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) it says there are 2 ways of removing a paradox condition, waiting for it to lapse <b>then</b> scouring it, or doing its special thing(summon monster, casting a spell with no paradox, or fully containing a paradox) which resolves the condition.<br /> <br /> If you still want to tighten the vice around your players tempt them with unwise but potentially rewarding choices, let events land together that at a glance look completely mundane or easy to handle then let things roll out of control. Be creative and don't be afraid to get down and dirty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11660-sleepychicken","name":"SleepyChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11660_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T10:59:56-08:00","id":1052059,"title":"","content":"Of note, I'm not running, I'm a player so I don't control any of the vices <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We're also going to play around with how to use severity of the Paradox, anyone done anything with them themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T11:09:47-08:00","id":1052061,"title":"","content":"I've always found it to be a little light on the downside. Are you ever running low or out of Mana?<br /> <br /> Have you raised your Gnosis much? The penalty for Reaching gets higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T11:26:17-08:00","id":1052066,"title":"","content":"The party is pretty uniformly Gnosis 3 so 2 paradox dice per excess Reach. Mana is...not usually an issue, between Legacy Oblations, Hallows, Tass and Scouring for Mana (and one player with an artifact that can store a lot) we're usually with a few in hand in case we need it.<br /> <br /> Mostly it's spent on me casting with Sympathy or for pushing mana into Mystery Investigation rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T20:08:25-08:00","id":1052360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052066#post1052066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The party is pretty uniformly Gnosis 3 so 2 paradox dice per excess Reach. Mana is...not usually an issue, between Legacy Oblations, Hallows, Tass and Scouring for Mana (and one player with an artifact that can store a lot) we're usually with a few in hand in case we need it.<br /> <br /> Mostly it's spent on me casting with Sympathy or for pushing mana into Mystery Investigation rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple things that will generally provide some traction on Mana demand to some degree: What's everybody's Wisdom looking like? And has anybody Inured any spells yet? How often is the presence of Sleepers an issue? What kind of Dedicated Tools are they making use of? What kind of Legacies are in play here and to what level of mastery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T04:44:13-08:00","id":1052498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1051657#post1051657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, Paradox only really became a severe problem when I forced my players into tight spaces. Combat, subterranean labyrinths, Space-warded extradimensional temples, places like that where you're counting every turn and damage is adding up.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much this. For someone like me who doesn't like combat in my games very often, Paradox is basically a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:05:37-08:00","id":1052594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052360#post1052360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple things that will generally provide some traction on Mana demand to some degree: What's everybody's Wisdom looking like? And has anybody Inured any spells yet? How often is the presence of Sleepers an issue? What kind of Dedicated Tools are they making use of? What kind of Legacies are in play here and to what level of mastery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wisdom is mostly 7, two players with 6 (both for killing a Seer, one killed them and the other encouraged him to do it). Personally I don't think the GM is pushing it hard enough but by and large the players are trying to retain Wisdom and avoid stuff overly harmful to others or too petty, unless Conditions get in the way!<br /> <br /> No spells Inured.<br /> <br /> Sleepers are an issue when we're out investigating but most action/tense scenes are away in Beast Lairs, Alternate Realms, the Shadow, Deep inside Infrastructure of the God Machine, or Seer holdings where they're trying to keep sleepers away for their own beenfit too etc. where sleepers aren't about.<br /> <br /> Legacies are all self created so only done at Gnosis 3. Mine gives me Kinetic Efficiency and the ability to activate Correspondence and maintain it so long as I concentrate on it (action for the round) so basic 1st level.<br /> <br /> Dedicated tools are mostly low profile (in at least one case explicitly because it made using it and carrying it easier...) while mine is the most difficult to use - it's a mask, the character is a Dancer based almost solely on the image of Yogo Kazunori","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 02-21-2017, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:15:31-08:00","id":1052616,"title":"","content":"Some follow-up questions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052594#post1052594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom is mostly 7, two players with 6 (both for killing a Seer, one killed them and the other encouraged him to do it). Personally I don't think the GM is pushing it hard enough but by and large the players are trying to retain Wisdom and avoid stuff overly harmful to others or too petty, unless Conditions get in the way!</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Conditions, did the two characters with Wisdom 6 take Megalomaniacal or Rampant, and have either of them discharged their Conditions yet?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sleepers are an issue when we're out investigating but most action/tense scenes are away in Beast Lairs, Alternate Realms, the Shadow, Deep inside Infrastructure of the God Machine, or Seer holdings where they're trying to keep sleepers away for their own beenfit too etc. where sleepers aren't about. </div> </div> </div>So between this and the longer timeframe you mentioned it's looking like long-term extradimensional/liminal exploration and similar activity is making up the bulk of your game's Mysteries. Any tangles with vampires or cults or other weird socially-oriented phenomena? How's the cabal's mundane lives looking in relation to all the lorediving they're doing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Legacies are all self created so only done at Gnosis 3. Mine gives me Kinetic Efficiency and the ability to activate Correspondence and maintain it so long as I concentrate on it (action for the round) so basic 1st level. </div> </div> </div>You mentioned that pretty much everyone's hit Adeptitude in an Arcanum and Oblations are making Mana easy enough to come by in the long term; what's the overlap like between those Arcana and the Legacies' extra Ruling numbers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dedicated tools are mostly low profile (in at least one case explicitly because it made using it and carrying it easier...) while mine is the most difficult to use - it's a mask, the character is a Dancer based almost solely on the image of Yogo Kazunori </div> </div> </div>Handy to know, and that does remind me that the Path and Order makeup of the cabal is probably also going to be helpful for piecing together viable reasons to risk Paradox, but my main reason for asking about Dedicated tools (and part of the reason I asked about Legacies) was semiotics; what kind of spells are y'all getting the full benefits of your chosen Instruments from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:20:45-08:00","id":1052770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless#post1051621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi,<br /> and the few times we've had Paradox it's been contained through Wisdom for a handful of resistant bashing damage</div> </div> </div> </div>Always thought it should be resistant aggravated damage. That'll make players <i>really </i>think if they want to contain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:57:10-08:00","id":1052865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052616#post1052616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some follow-up questions:<br /> <br /> Speaking of Conditions, did the two characters with Wisdom 6 take Megalomaniacal or Rampant, and have either of them discharged their Conditions yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>The one who convinced th eother player to kill the Seer took Rampant - they imposed their will and got their way and now they feel able to do it again. They discharged it but rather enjoyed having an excuse for being indiscriminate (they risked another breaking point but passed it). The player who actually killed them took Guilty as it seemed more relevant at the time, as far as I know that still remains (Guilty seems a really tough one to clear in general actually...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052616#post1052616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So between this and the longer timeframe you mentioned it's looking like long-term extradimensional/liminal exploration and similar activity is making up the bulk of your game's Mysteries. Any tangles with vampires or cults or other weird socially-oriented phenomena? How's the cabal's mundane lives looking in relation to all the lorediving they're doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly yes, we're in a hub city where the previous Consilium has fallen apart and the surrounding areas are also falling apart under the presures of Seer activity (that might be coordinated, we don't know for sure but suspect). The collapse of the Consilium in the city and deaths and failings of the mages in there has led to much damage and escaping of experiments, oddities, unchecked magic going haywire, etc. and we're stuck right in the middle of it.<br /> <br /> Basically we're hopping from one bit of weirdness to the next going off and untangling some mages foibles and fall outs and fixing what we can.<br /> <br /> Limited social interaction but we had a meeting with some Vampires last session - some incestuous small grouping in a small city where they were all bonded through blood to the leading family members. However the Time focused Mage 'Oracle' rolled a crazy 10 successes on a freak roll with her praxis to see the future of the meeting, checking to see what threats awaited us. So we played out the scene inside her vision to prep ourselves and kind of evaded most of the risk there (GM basically decided that when a player rolls 10 successes on the thing they made as the crux of their character they should win pretty big and not screw it over!).<br /> <br /> Outside of that mortal lives aren't a major factor. Mine has briefly come up (character used to be in mental health care as they had strange visions all through their life until they finally awakened and the character realised what they had been seeing glimpses of all along...the health authorities were less convinced when he told them he was actually a wizard and not hallucinating at all...honest!) but some bribery in the right places from the Silver Ladder rich guy in the group deflected that by and large.<br /> <br /> The Moros has been rebuliding connections with military friends and associates from their mortal life and trying to find the ghosts of fallen comrades.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052616#post1052616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mentioned that pretty much everyone's hit Adeptitude in an Arcanum and Oblations are making Mana easy enough to come by in the long term; what's the overlap like between those Arcana and the Legacies' extra Ruling numbers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people have used their Legacy to get a third ruling - arguably cheesy but obviously expected as it's called out in the Legacy section as a thing to do. Mana used to be more of an issue (especially for me, I gained Space as a third ruling - started Obrimos - and casting sympathetically was very expensive prior to that).<br /> <br /> Actually that's probably a big part of why mana is less of an issue now. XPwise pushing three Arcana to strong levels is costly so by this point the bulk of casting will be done using their three preferred arcana whereas before people would have had one of their preferred arcana as non-ruling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052616#post1052616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Handy to know, and that does remind me that the Path and Order makeup of the cabal is probably also going to be helpful for piecing together viable reasons to risk Paradox, but my main reason for asking about Dedicated tools (and part of the reason I asked about Legacies) was semiotics; what kind of spells are y'all getting the full benefits of your chosen Instruments from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure we have one of each Path. No one is a Guardian but we have two Silver Ladder. Not certain about what everyone gets but 'Oracle' gets it on spells to reveal hidden things and for seeing the future (funny that...), the Thyrsus is getting it on spells to alter the bosy (growing gills, buffing strength, etc.) and I am getting it on things to do with motion and physically traversing space (teleporting doesn't count) as I am 'The Dancer' - schtick is treating sympathetic threads as literal strings like on an instrument, pluck them to make music and dancing to the music of the world around me and through that 'divine dance' travel along sympathetic threads (hence Forces and Space as my focus, movement/sound and traversal).<br /> <br /> I know a Mask doesn't really line up with what I have it do but I designed the character from an image first so we bent things a little to make it fit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/l5r/images/9/90/Yogo_Kazunori.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20130120181914\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/l5r/images/9/90/Yogo_Kazunori.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20130120181914\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/l5r/images/9/90/Yogo_Kazunori.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20130120181914\" target=\"_blank\"> http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/l5r/images/9/90/Yogo_Kazunori.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20130120181914 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And yes to claim my Shadow Name benefits I have to dress in the loose flowing robes and dance...I don't tend to get the Shadow Name benefits very often <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:49:24-08:00","id":1052940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052865#post1052865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The player who actually killed them took Guilty as it seemed more relevant at the time, as far as I know that still remains (Guilty seems a really tough one to clear in general actually...).</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, that's kind of bending the rules re: how Acts of Hubris impact mage psychology.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, restitution to the Seers seems an ample opportunity for social complications. Know if they've got a plan for that or are they just letting the Condition ride for now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mostly yes, we're in a hub city where the previous Consilium has fallen apart and the surrounding areas are also falling apart under the presures of Seer activity (that might be coordinated, we don't know for sure but suspect). The collapse of the Consilium in the city and deaths and failings of the mages in there has led to much damage and escaping of experiments, oddities, unchecked magic going haywire, etc. and we're stuck right in the middle of it. </div> </div> </div>What's the over/under on Abyssal shenanigans caused or attracted by that much magic on the loose? (Relatedly, what's been the Seer response to such, given the institutional demands of that Sect?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Limited social interaction but we had a meeting with some Vampires last session - some incestuous small grouping in a small city where they were all bonded through blood to the leading family members. </div> </div> </div>Out of the way from the rest of the cabal's activities, or do these guys seem likely to recur somewhere down the line?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Outside of that mortal lives aren't a major factor. </div> </div> </div>Accordingly, what're the cabal's sympathies to their magical lives looking like, just going off of things that have come up in the narrative? (Also, how's maintaining the fidelity of Shadow Name separation been so far?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most people have used their Legacy to get a third ruling - arguably cheesy but obviously expected as it's called out in the Legacy section as a thing to do. Mana used to be more of an issue (especially for me, I gained Space as a third ruling - started Obrimos - and casting sympathetically was very expensive prior to that).<br /> <br /> Actually that's probably a big part of why mana is less of an issue now. XPwise pushing three Arcana to strong levels is costly so by this point the bulk of casting will be done using their three preferred arcana whereas before people would have had one of their preferred arcana as non-ruling. </div> </div> </div>So pretty much everybody's rocking their third Ruling Arcanum to the limit of their Gnosis at the moment, it seems. What kind of Legacy symbolism have we got on the table here?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not certain about what everyone gets </div> </div> </div>I should clarify that that was a circumlocutory means of asking what the Dedicated Tools in question were.<br /> <br /> Is the Mastigos one of the Silver Ladder folks? Also, is the cabal generally lumping together to tackle the concern du jour as a group, or does splitting up to tackle multiple angles happen with some regularity? (Relatedly, has anyone got familiars or Retainers or other extra pairs of handlike appendages at their disposal? What's everyone's Status looking like?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T13:54:05-08:00","id":1053410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052940#post1052940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, that's kind of bending the rules re: how Acts of Hubris impact mage psychology.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, restitution to the Seers seems an ample opportunity for social complications. Know if they've got a plan for that or are they just letting the Condition ride for now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're just riding it, mostly because they don't want to deal with the complications resolving it would cause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052940#post1052940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the over/under on Abyssal shenanigans caused or attracted by that much magic on the loose? (Relatedly, what's been the Seer response to such, given the institutional demands of that Sect?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal stuff is slowly appearing more often as spells and the like are degrading and allowing more and more in. Seers themselves are actively dealing with Abysal (or other) entities that are getting too far loose but it seems like they're trying to corral them on top of us rather than jumping us directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052940#post1052940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of the way from the rest of the cabal's activities, or do these guys seem likely to recur somewhere down the line?</div> </div> </div> </div>They mostly wanted us to leave them alone and they're kind of out of the main area we're operating in so inlikely to come up much (unless the GM is planning stuff nefariously we're yet to realise).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052940#post1052940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Accordingly, what're the cabal's sympathies to their magical lives looking like, just going off of things that have come up in the narrative? (Also, how's maintaining the fidelity of Shadow Name separation been so far?)</div> </div> </div> </div>In general we're being Mages and focusing on Mage stuff. Mortal lives rarely intrude. Most people are always getting their Shadow Names and Nimbuses should be starting to be a strong trail to follow on to us. Technically family and friends should be in danger but we've not seen that if it's going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052940#post1052940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So pretty much everybody's rocking their third Ruling Arcanum to the limit of their Gnosis at the moment, it seems. What kind of Legacy symbolism have we got on the table here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will have to check with the other players but one Arcana at 4, a second at 3 and then one or two others at 1 to 2 is I suspect the standard across the cabal. Legacy symbolism is diverse and very much of the 'make me better at what I was going to do anyway' hence everyone founding their own legacies.<br /> <br /> Oracle is very much the traditional Norns or Fates, glimpse the future and weave threads of Fate. The Mastigos is taking cues from an older Silver Ladder legacy (from the SL book, using Fate for wealth and pefect looks) who is impeccably perfect. Will need to check with the Thyrsus and Moros about theirs while I - like I mentioned prior - treat sympathetic threads as literal physical things that can be spun and plucked used to make music.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052940#post1052940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should clarify that that was a circumlocutory means of asking what the Dedicated Tools in question were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Coin taken from a historical dig site, a metal camping cup polished to a perfect shine, a steel rod with lead filligree, my masks and I think the last is a set of small carved wooden animals on a necklace thong (either the dedicated or the one they find the most useful as they use it all the time)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1052940#post1052940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Mastigos one of the Silver Ladder folks? Also, is the cabal generally lumping together to tackle the concern du jour as a group, or does splitting up to tackle multiple angles happen with some regularity? (Relatedly, has anyone got familiars or Retainers or other extra pairs of handlike appendages at their disposal? What's everyone's Status looking like?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes myself and the Mastigos are Silver Ladder, he has greater Status than me with them.<br /> <br /> Cabal doesn't split up if it can avoid it. To the point where I will often Co-Locate (space 3) us if we have to to avoid getting into trouble alone. To the point where we'd rather risk assess and tackle highest priority and allow other things to go wrong than spread out and leave ourselves vulnerable (clues are making us feel actively hunted, likely by the Seers corraling things).<br /> <br /> The Moros has got a Retainer as a Ghost he's slowly growing as he helps it become more lucid. I have a Mentor and a Mystery Cult Influence (technically the Mentor's Cult and I am a senior figure) but that's mostly a 4 dot way of getting 1 dot of (University Cultists) Staff who have never been used. Moros (ex military) and Mastigos (wealthy busines entrepeneur) want to start a supernatural PMC based on the kinds of conspiracies in the Hunter book so they've been working towards buying/justifying story for the first dots of that.<br /> <br /> Status is low, rank 1 mostly. The Mastigos Silver Ladder is about 3 though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:53:04-08:00","id":1053435,"title":"","content":"You could always use the less orthodox reading of the Cumulative Paradox rule. Basically, rule isn't very clear if it talks about adding +1 Paradox Dice per Paradox Risked in the scene to All Spells, or to spells that risk Paradox &quot;to begin with&quot;. I like the unpopular ruling, mostly because it allows risk generation even in slow scenes (scenes can be long) instead of making pretty much &quot;intense action scenes only&quot;. It also introduces a soft limit on a number of times you can try something - if you risked Paradox at least once in a scene, you can't really fish for Praxis in order to mana regen because each fishing attempt will bloat the paradox risk. <br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> For reference, page 115 of core rulebook. Dice Modifiers table, third entry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:51:38-08:00","id":1053508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053410#post1053410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal stuff is slowly appearing more often as spells and the like are degrading and allowing more and more in. Seers themselves are actively dealing with Abysal (or other) entities that are getting too far loose but it seems like they're trying to corral them on top of us rather than jumping us directly.<br /> <br /> In general we're being Mages and focusing on Mage stuff. Mortal lives rarely intrude. Most people are always getting their Shadow Names and Nimbuses should be starting to be a strong trail to follow on to us. Technically family and friends should be in danger but we've not seen that if it's going on.<br /> <br /> Cabal doesn't split up if it can avoid it. To the point where I will often Co-Locate (space 3) us if we have to to avoid getting into trouble alone. To the point where we'd rather risk assess and tackle highest priority and allow other things to go wrong than spread out and leave ourselves vulnerable (clues are making us feel actively hunted, likely by the Seers corraling things).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a need to lay low in your nonmagical identities could help substantially with making Paradox a more present concern, particularly if a lot of your Shadow Names are invested to the point of Merit dots. Abyssal pseudocult activity is probably also going to be tough to handle if allowed to fester, and that kind of stuff thrives on Sleepers.<br /> <br /> It's easy to fall into the lull of ignoring the mortal world in a supernaturally-focused game, but that kind of grounding taken in combination with the scale of the Orders relative to their Awakened membership bears remembering for the purposes of having the game run well with the assumptions that're baked into it. For now, the cabal's Strong and Medium sympathies to their magical lives should probably have the effects of the Nimbus considered in the larger scheme of things \u2014 particularly speaking, have any of them got any long-term spells sitting around and/or weighing on their control limits?<br /> <br /> Also, while we're on the subject of sympathies: Have you got a usual approach for the Yantras you use for Space magic? (Co-Location in particular is pretty dependent upon that, location-based spell that it is.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Moros has got a Retainer as a Ghost he's slowly growing as he helps it become more lucid. I have a Mentor and a Mystery Cult Influence (technically the Mentor's Cult and I am a senior figure) but that's mostly a 4 dot way of getting 1 dot of (University Cultists) Staff who have never been used. Moros (ex military) and Mastigos (wealthy busines entrepeneur) want to start a supernatural PMC based on the kinds of conspiracies in the Hunter book so they've been working towards buying/justifying story for the first dots of that.<br /> <br /> Status is low, rank 1 mostly. The Mastigos Silver Ladder is about 3 though. </div> </div> </div>This is a bit afield, but are any of the cabal looking to expand their Legacies as they develop them? Depending on the nature of the Moros's soulcrafting, that might serve them well in growing the PMC.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, am I reading it correctly that your own Legacy is intended partially as an extension of your Shadow Name? If so, does that tie back to the Mentor or the Cult at all?<br /> <br /> <br /> (I must confess I'm partially mining for information out of curiosity, but these things do provide a lot of knobs and dials for refining the story and play experience, so thank you for your patience with this battery of questions.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T03:21:53-08:00","id":1053732,"title":"","content":"Paradox is just luring you into a false sense of security. Eventually, you're going to see it as a non-issue and get careless...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T08:08:04-08:00","id":1053822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053732#post1053732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox is just luring you into a false sense of security. Eventually, you're going to see it as a non-issue and get careless...</div> </div> </div> </div>In the end its going to rely on the Storyteller. Make your own Paradox Condition or Tilt, fiddle with Reach. If the Storyteller's going easy on the players there's no reason to expect them to suddenly slam them with a harsh Paradox result.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T13:28:37-08:00","id":1053978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053435#post1053435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always use the less orthodox reading of the Cumulative Paradox rule. Basically, rule isn't very clear if it talks about adding +1 Paradox Dice per Paradox Risked in the scene to All Spells, or to spells that risk Paradox &quot;to begin with&quot;. I like the unpopular ruling, mostly because it allows risk generation even in slow scenes (scenes can be long) instead of making pretty much &quot;intense action scenes only&quot;. It also introduces a soft limit on a number of times you can try something - if you risked Paradox at least once in a scene, you can't really fish for Praxis in order to mana regen because each fishing attempt will bloat the paradox risk.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> For reference, page 115 of core rulebook. Dice Modifiers table, third entry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We didn't realise there was even a different reading...we all assumed and have been playing that after casting ANY spell with Paradox ALL spells in the scene (by that Mage) then gain the +1 cumulative Paradox, which means you are always causing Paradox from then on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053508#post1053508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a need to lay low in your nonmagical identities could help substantially with making Paradox a more present concern, particularly if a lot of your Shadow Names are invested to the point of Merit dots. Abyssal pseudocult activity is probably also going to be tough to handle if allowed to fester, and that kind of stuff thrives on Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be in the future for us, I'll mention it to the GM and see if I get a knowing look or pleasant surprise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053508#post1053508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy to fall into the lull of ignoring the mortal world in a supernaturally-focused game, but that kind of grounding taken in combination with the scale of the Orders relative to their Awakened membership bears remembering for the purposes of having the game run well with the assumptions that're baked into it. For now, the cabal's Strong and Medium sympathies to their magical lives should probably have the effects of the Nimbus considered in the larger scheme of things \u2014 particularly speaking, have any of them got any long-term spells sitting around and/or weighing on their control limits?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do yes, mostly self buffing though. A silly high ritual casting for bonus armour on 5 kevlar jackets (for us to wear), a year long mental shield on the Mastigos and the Thyrsus has a monthly refreshed buff to raise their Strength and Dex by 3-4 points. Not really leaving spells lying around away from us though and they're all sitting in our Gnosis 3 spells within limits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053508#post1053508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while we're on the subject of sympathies: Have you got a usual approach for the Yantras you use for Space magic? (Co-Location in particular is pretty dependent upon that, location-based spell that it is.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I collect something useful from most of the key locations we visit and keep those in a storage container a hour or so away from our Sanctum. I have a keyring with a knot of hair from each Cabal mate too which I use to colocate them with me when they are away from me (or does Co-Locate need a link to the physical location and not the people at that location?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053508#post1053508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a bit afield, but are any of the cabal looking to expand their Legacies as they develop them? Depending on the nature of the Moros's soulcrafting, that might serve them well in growing the PMC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure, I can ask. I suspect though that they're going to be keeping on with the 'bonus to what I was going to do anyway' theme rather than drastically evolve who they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053508#post1053508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relatedly, am I reading it correctly that your own Legacy is intended partially as an extension of your Shadow Name? If so, does that tie back to the Mentor or the Cult at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, character was, prior to awakening, suffering visions and hallucinations (i.e.: basically stuck in a years long Shadow Play) and was considered mentally unwell and taken into health care, drugged and dealing with the stigmas attached. They did not have particularly strong connections to who they were prior to being a Mage but after Awakening they flowered into confidence and found acceptance in a way they'd never had before. The bits of Silver Ladder philosophy that espouse magic as humans birthright and something you should be able to use without fear of the abyss appealed. The Legacy is more soul crafting in the things they'd grown up seeing and then suppressing with drugs, hearing strange music and shimmering threads connecting things. Basically, as far as the character is concerned, they ARE their Shadow Name and who they were before is some drug addled false chrysalis stage. So yeah, Leagcy is very much the Shadow Name.<br /> <br /> Mortal side is mostly health care professionals and family who - as far as they know - have someone suffering delusions and hallicinations who has disappeared and gone off medication. I have a tailored/tweaked version of Surveilled from Demon to represent that (it triggered once already which was bribed away by the Mastigos).<br /> <br /> (OOC: a lot of that is because I wanted to play a <i>Mage</i> rather than the regular person so made the character emotinally attached to that side more than the mortal side, also weird and completely ungrounded in normal concerns)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T21:22:14-08:00","id":1054186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1053978#post1053978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do yes, mostly self buffing though. A silly high ritual casting for bonus armour on 5 kevlar jackets (for us to wear), a year long mental shield on the Mastigos and the Thyrsus has a monthly refreshed buff to raise their Strength and Dex by 3-4 points. Not really leaving spells lying around away from us though and they're all sitting in our Gnosis 3 spells within limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me: What's the Sanctum situation looking like? Single shared quarters? Individual ritual spaces? How much spell is being stored for safekeeping in there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I collect something useful from most of the key locations we visit and keep those in a storage container a hour or so away from our Sanctum. I have a keyring with a knot of hair from each Cabal mate too which I use to colocate them with me when they are away from me (or does Co-Locate need a link to the physical location and not the people at that location?). </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, particularly if you or the Mastigos maintain decent sympathy to the strongbox. (I'm reasonably certain Co-Location specifically works on concrete locations rather than the variable &quot;wherever this non-place-noun is&quot; coordinates \u2014 &quot;bring these subjects together&quot; magic is more definitely the domain of Teleportation, which I am guessing is within your bailiwick but might not be if your Adeptitude is in Forces or Prime instead.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure, I can ask. I suspect though that they're going to be keeping on with the 'bonus to what I was going to do anyway' theme rather than drastically evolve who they are. </div> </div> </div>I really need to get better at saying what I mean: Do any of them plan on taking students anywhere down the road once they've developed their third Attainment after Gnosis 5, given the delicious delicious Arcane Beats they can provide? (Relatedly, what're the cabal's Praxes in play?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OOC: a lot of that is because I wanted to play a <i>Mage</i> rather than the regular person so made the character emotinally attached to that side more than the mortal side, also weird and completely ungrounded in normal concerns) </div> </div> </div>Completely understandable, though it's probably worth remembering that the gradual disconnection from mortal affairs is a pretty rich ground for storytelling fodder in the early to middle stages of being-a-mage (to say nothing of the utility of mundane life as mystical cover) \u2014 racing to the back of the Gnosis chart or similarly diving whole-hog into the Mysteries tends to crank the stakes up at a rate that makes death or Wisdom loss more likely. (Sense of urgency is the biggest tool in the ST's bag for this and I'd recommend they keep it in mind if they're looking to give Paradox more weight.)<br /> <br /> Speaking of chasing dragons' tails: What kind of Obsessions are on the table at present? How much alignment is there between them and the cabal's activities as a group? (And contrariwise, how much conflict is there between same?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:13:36-08:00","id":1054874,"title":"","content":"Next session is tomorrow, discussed some of the stuff from this thread with the GM, we'll see how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T12:30:40-08:00","id":1054911,"title":"","content":"Small pause in a session for me. We just finished a fight with an Acamoth who used Influence: Paradox to give us &quot;bonus&quot; dice and caused every spell to suffer Paradox. I managed to get up to 6 extra Paradox dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T06:04:07-08:00","id":1056077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1054911#post1054911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small pause in a session for me. We just finished a fight with an Acamoth who used Influence: Paradox to give us &amp;quot;bonus&amp;quot; dice and caused every spell to suffer Paradox. I managed to get up to 6 extra Paradox dice.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is a great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:17:02-08:00","id":1056095,"title":"","content":"It's not often a mage manages to get six Paradox dice in his own Oneiros. A previous session had the rest of the Cabal (my character was basically comatose after a major fuck up that led to both of these incidents) pitted against one Acamoth and one Gulmoth inside my character's Oneiros, and either the general Abyssal presence or a power activated by one of the entities led to all present mages to share &quot;Doom Counters&quot;. Our ST hands out one glass counter everytime a spell has to check for Paradox. That led to a record high of 8 Paradox counters.<br /> <br /> Edit: So there's two ways of making Paradox a whole lot worse, but not applicable in most situations. But great ideas for handling Abyssal entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-28-2017, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T00:30:10-08:00","id":1061153,"title":"","content":"Currenlty airing anime Little Witch Academia shows a lot how Dramatic Failures on Spellcasting and Paradox can make Mage game fun while also progressing character arcs and not necessarily just act as story derailing punishments. Do Paradox in that way and players will be tempted to Dramatic Failure that Failure and will be more willing to not do everything they can to overpower Paradoxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T10:59:31-08:00","id":1061290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061153#post1061153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currenlty airing anime Little Witch Academia shows a lot how Dramatic Failures on Spellcasting and Paradox can make Mage game fun while also progressing character arcs and not necessarily just act as story derailing punishments. Do Paradox in that way and players will be tempted to Dramatic Failure that Failure and will be more willing to not do everything they can to overpower Paradoxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I find Paradox to be much more interesting and to come up a lot more when it isn't used as a punishment stick. While Paradox can and should end disastrously every now and then, to do so every time (or even most of the time, really) makes it way too predictable. Yes, Paraadox warps and twists a spell, changing it from how the casting mage originally designed it, but who's to say that those changes can't be beneficial? Increased Potency, targeting even more of a mages enemies than said mage was able to do without it, etc. IMO Paradox shouldn't be a punishment, it should be another temptation. Scelesti exist for a reason. The Abyss is another, albeit dangerous, path to power and showing that Paradox can help you as much as it screws you over goes a long way into proving that. <br /> <br /> And even when you do use it to screw players over, do your best to make it <i>interesting.</i> Make them look forward to seeing what happens next, not dread how they know they're about to get screwed again. It'll make your players a lot more willing to let Paradox fly rather than stifling it every time, and with it usually being just as useful as it is not, when it comes time to hit them with a <i>really</i> nasty one then it'll be one to remember rather than just the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T12:10:24-08:00","id":1061308,"title":"","content":"This might have already been suggested, but removing the penalty to spellcasting rolls would make Paradox much more tempting to release, I think. Haven't tried it in my game yet, but I'm heavily considering it to see how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T13:48:59-08:00","id":1061332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061153#post1061153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currenlty airing anime Little Witch Academia</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, that got an anime? Not just the movies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T20:48:07-08:00","id":1061430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061308#post1061308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have already been suggested, but removing the penalty to spellcasting rolls would make Paradox much more tempting to release, I think. Haven't tried it in my game yet, but I'm heavily considering it to see how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the first thing I did, yeah, because I <i>want</i> my players to release Paradoxes' instead of just containing them all the time. I've pondered adding a Damage Factor, or whatever the autodamage that gets added to attacks with weapons, to the damage you take from containing too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T21:08:00-08:00","id":1061437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061430#post1061430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was the first thing I did, yeah, because I <i>want</i> my players to release Paradoxes' instead of just containing them all the time. I've pondered adding a Damage Factor, or whatever the autodamage that gets added to attacks with weapons, to the damage you take from containing too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, containing a Paradox is the way you get the Abyss inside you corrupting you in ways you can't detect as easily,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T21:34:51-08:00","id":1061445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061437#post1061437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, containing a Paradox is the way you get the Abyss inside you corrupting you in ways you can't detect as easily,</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, time pressure and resource investment are the only things stopping you from just trying the spell again besides suspendible concern for your surroundings \u2014 the most common consequence releasing a Paradox can inflict is imprecision on a spell you can terminate by virtue of it being on your control, and the principal way around that problem is giving the characters a reason to not care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T09:34:03-07:00","id":1061560,"title":"","content":"Yeah, people get way too hung up on wanting to ruin their player's magic as if that's where the ST is supposed to get his jollies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T02:33:37-07:00","id":1061767,"title":"","content":"I think releasing vs containing should be a strategic choice. Of course, conditions like Megalomanaical and Rampant provide incentives, but they don't <i>force</i> the player to release. I can't really think of what circumstances would make a normal player decide to release, unless they're already pretty injured. Also, I don't think the penalizing of spellcasting rolls really does anything for the system, as the ST having control over what happens to the spell is already anomalous enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T03:34:17-07:00","id":1061772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061767#post1061767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really think of what circumstances would make a normal player decide to release, unless they're already pretty injured.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you have low Wisdom you're less likely to succeed at containing a Paradox, if you try and fail then you have a very limited amount of time to resolve the Paradox Condition, if you fail at that then you need to Scour. Releasing becomes the safer option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T08:38:25-07:00","id":1061838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061767#post1061767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't think the penalizing of spellcasting rolls really does anything for the system</div> </div> </div> </div>It's potential extra Reach. A -1 to the casting roll is a small price to pay for extra Scale or Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T13:18:44-07:00","id":1062451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1061838#post1061838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's potential extra Reach. A -1 to the casting roll is a small price to pay for extra Scale or Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's assuming you're using Abyssal spellcasting to control the Reach. Otherwise the ST might give you some random Paradox Reach effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T13:35:00-07:00","id":1062459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062451#post1062451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's assuming you're using Abyssal spellcasting to control the Reach. Otherwise the ST might give you some random Paradox Reach effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>-1 to the casting means the ST has one Paradox Reach to allocate. The only option available at that level is toggling Advanced Factors on or off. When you maintain control over the spell until it's relinquished and releasing a Paradox explicitly doesn't have to negatively impact the desired outcome whether you taint the casting or not.<br /> <br /> For an instant-cast spell with no Reaches put into Spell Factors, that means a chance of Advanced Potency, Advanced Duration, Advanced Scale, or Sensory Range. As outcomes go, that's <i>potentially sloppy</i>, not <i>disastrous</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Apply a Condition to the subject of the spell&quot; isn't that much worse by default either, really, particularly given the relation of self-applied Conditions to the Beat economy; it's Abyssal Environmental Tilts and gulmoth-summoning that're the ones to watch out for, and the risk of those is relatively small early on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T15:50:26-07:00","id":1062513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062459#post1062459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-1 to the casting means the ST has one Paradox Reach to allocate.<br /> <br /> &quot;Apply a Condition to the subject of the spell&quot; isn't that much worse by default either, really, particularly given the relation of self-applied Conditions to the Beat economy; it's Abyssal Environmental Tilts and gulmoth-summoning that're the ones to watch out for, and the risk of those is relatively small early on.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Not much worse&quot; is somewhat iffy, isn't it? It's a Condition. Not &quot;one of these Conditions here,&quot; if my reading is correct, but any &quot;you now live in interesting times&quot; Condition the Storyteller chooses to inflict. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062459#post1062459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an instant-cast spell with no Reaches put into Spell Factors, that means a chance of Advanced Potency, Advanced Duration, Advanced Scale, or Sensory Range. As outcomes go, that's <i>potentially sloppy</i>, not <i>disastrous</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ostensibly, the Storyteller gets to make all the choices this Reach application needs.<br /> <br /> If you're casting on a foe, Advanced Scale bumps the spell from &quot;this one dude&quot; to &quot;these five dudes,&quot;(if you're casting at Sensory) or more amusingly, area of &quot;a large house or building&quot; including the cabal, or innocent passers-by.<br /> If you're casting on a friend or self, Advanced Scale, like above, can include foes among the targets.<br /> <br /> The random folk affected could then have not so happy Integrity times, in addition to being unwantedly affected by the spell. <br /> <br /> And that's if you have just one Reach to spend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T16:25:47-07:00","id":1062538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062513#post1062513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Not much worse&quot; is somewhat iffy, isn't it? It's a Condition. Not &quot;one of these Conditions here,&quot; if my reading is correct, but any &quot;you now live in interesting times&quot; Condition the Storyteller chooses to inflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, again, <i>releasing a Paradox is not supposed to be automatically ruinous to the character</i>. That's the point of the option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're casting on a foe, Advanced Scale bumps the spell from &quot;this one dude&quot; to &quot;these five dudes,&quot;(if you're casting at Sensory) or more amusingly, area of &quot;a large house or building&quot; including the cabal, or innocent passers-by.<br /> If you're casting on a friend or self, Advanced Scale, like above, can include foes among the targets. </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> Again, Spell Control means this is a <i>minor inconvenience</i> in most circumstances:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once a spell is cast, the mage can do very little to alter it. She cannot increase the spell factors short of canceling the spell and recasting it, though <b>she can restrict its effects by reducing factors such as Potency, Duration, or Scale. As an instant action, the mage can reduce the factors of one of her spells in any way she chooses, </b>but although <b>she can reduce the number of subjects if the spell used that form of Scale</b>, all spell factors must still apply equally to all subjects \u2013 she can\u2019t weaken a spell for a specific individual without further magic. <b>A mage may cancel any of her active spells as a reflexive action.</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The random folk affected could then have not so happy Integrity times, in addition to being unwantedly affected by the spell. </div> </div> </div>This is yet another reason mages don't favor the blasto-magic approach to conflict resolution, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's if you have just one Reach to spend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Contrariwise, in a Sanctum or other isolated location, there's little reason not to cast and re-cast a self-buff over and over until you get a favorable result \u2014 that's how Praxes already work, after all, and half the basis of rotes being the means by which a Master pushes their limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T22:40:16-07:00","id":1062667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062538#post1062538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, <i>releasing a Paradox is not supposed to be automatically ruinous to the character</i>. That's the point of the option.<br /> <br /> Yup.<br /> <br /> Again, Spell Control means this is a <i>minor inconvenience</i> in most circumstances:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is yet another reason mages don't favor the blasto-magic approach to conflict resolution, yes.<br /> <br /> Contrariwise, in a Sanctum or other isolated location, there's little reason not to cast and re-cast a self-buff over and over until you get a favorable result \u2014 that's how Praxes already work, after all, and half the basis of rotes being the means by which a Master pushes their limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>We agree on most things here, if not outright all.<br /> <br /> Just saying Paradox can be interesting when things get tight, even with just a single Reach available. Whether that means it's not toothless or it just amuses itself in less toothy ways is open to be played with.<br /> <br /> If the Mage is under no time/resource pressure, yeah, prepare properly. Otherwise risk Paradox and hope for the best.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also wondering now, does the Condition end when the spell ends by default? It's not the spell effect itself, the Condition inflicted on the target could stay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T23:20:55-07:00","id":1062680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062667#post1062667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also wondering now, does the Condition end when the spell ends by default? It's not the spell effect itself, the Condition inflicted on the target could stay?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect it's subject to the Anomaly Duration chart just as the more extreme versions are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T07:58:07-07:00","id":1062791,"title":"","content":"I kind of want to run the game without the option to contain a paradox and see what happens.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T11:03:46-07:00","id":1062866,"title":"","content":"The weird thing is how paradox has decreasing returns with containing being a thing. You will never take more than 1L for scouring + (Successes on the Wisdom Roll)B damage.<br /> <br /> This means, e.g. You can use Shifting Sands to go back as far as you want with minimal consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-15-2017, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T12:01:29-07:00","id":1062898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062866#post1062866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird thing is how paradox has decreasing returns with containing being a thing. You will never take more than 1L for scouring + (Successes on the Wisdom Roll)B damage.<br /> <br /> This means, e.g. You can use Shifting Sands to go back as far as you want with minimal consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1051731#post1051731\">&quot;Minimal.&quot;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T12:18:50-07:00","id":1062910,"title":"","content":"Pretty much only times when we see Releasing Paradox is in case of character that explicitly wants to be Low Wisdom selfish princess teenager character, who hates idea of feeling pain and is self taught Nameless Mage. It leads mostly to frustration due to having to constantly sacrifice two or three dice on &quot;safety wrapping&quot; so the spells will have a sensible chance to success. Which means people also never want to risk Releasing Paradox when they can't just the spell over and over, for example in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T13:14:16-07:00","id":1062944,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's like whining that you are not a good weight lifter by RAW. You are not suppose to but you can take some skill dots, merits and be &quot;this guy who lifts refrigerator above head&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T13:41:06-07:00","id":1062958,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Paradox Conditions in the latest version of the pdf list scouring them as a a way to resolve them specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-15-2017, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T13:54:22-07:00","id":1062961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062958#post1062958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Paradox Conditions in the latest version of the pdf list scouring them as a a way to resolve them specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>He knows that, but note you can only Scour -after- letting the Condition lapse which takes a variable amount of time depending on Wisdom. In other words, yes you could go back as far as you want with Shifting Sands, but if you insisted on Scouring the resulting Paradox Condition then you'd have to wait a certain amount of time in order for it lapse first during which time you'd be saddled with the Paradox Condition. So yes, 1 L + X B, but also Paradox Condition for the duration -that's- the minimal cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-15-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T14:00:14-07:00","id":1062964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051621-paradox-toothless?p=1062958#post1062958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Paradox Conditions in the latest version of the pdf list scouring them as a a way to resolve them specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'm saying that's pretty evidently an error, because the introductory paragraph only lists lapsing and the specific criterion of a particular Condition as means of resolution and there's otherwise no actual point in scaling their Duration.<br /> <br /> The errata pass missed some stuff (Ghost Shield's Primary Factor is consistent with the broad Protection guideline in the Creative Thaumaturgy process but inconsistent with Mental Shield's and Ephemeral Shield's Primary Factors despite their base functions being mechanically near-identical, for instance), which is to be expected when you're dealing with a 350-page book with lots of interconnected systems. It's necessary to use some critical thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}